# Autosave in steps (server/README.md "Autosave in steps"). Owner request: "Optimize the autosave time. Keep the
# warnings." The stock hourly save wrote every online player and every house in one dispatcher task: the game stood
# still for the whole save (1.2-1.4 s with 200 players, about 2.1-2.5 s at 400), and the backup's SIGUSR1 save did the same.
#   * Game::saveIncremental / Lua Game.saveIncremental([playersPerTick = 10[, tickBudgetMs = 25[, tickDelayMs = 50
#     [, housesPerTick = 100]]]]): the account storage in the first tick, then the online players one by one while
#     the tick's budget allows (at most playersPerTick, and another player only when the time so far plus the last
#     player's time fits tickBudgetMs), then the changed houses, with tickDelayMs (the scheduler's 50 ms minimum)
#     between ticks so the game runs in between. Each player save is the stock IOLoginData::savePlayer (one
#     transaction per player), so player:save() and the "save before credit" rule (Chaos.saveCharacter) keep their
#     meaning. A player who logs out before his turn was saved by the logout; one who logs in during the pass is not
#     in it. No game state change: no maintenance state, a closed server stays closed. False while a pass runs.
#     Game.isSaving(). One console line at the end: players saved, logged out, failed, houses, ticks, longest tick,
#     total time. A shutdown during a pass ends it (the shutdown saves everything).
#   * SIGUSR1 (server/tools/backup.sh) starts the same pass instead of the full save.
#   * Houses: Map::save (the full save of a shutdown, a closed server, /save, saveServer()) and the pass write only
#     the houses whose database rows differ from memory: the `houses` row (owner, paid, warnings, name, town, rent,
#     size, beds), the guest / subowner / door lists, the `tile_store` rows (anything on the house tiles: items added,
#     removed, moved or changed, container contents, texts, beds). Compared by content (an FNV-1a signature of the
#     sorted rows), so no change slips past a missed event. At startup loadHouseInfo / loadHouseItems record what the
#     database holds per house, so the first save after a start writes only what differs; a database that could not
#     be read (a new one) makes the first save write every house. One transaction per save (per chunk of
#     housesPerTick in the pass) with one INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE for the rows and one DELETE + INSERT for
#     the lists and the tile rows of the changed houses; rows of houses the map no longer has are deleted by the first
#     save, as the stock full rewrite did. A failed write marks those houses unknown (written in full next time);
#     house:save() keeps the record in step. A crash loses what it lost before: the changes since the last save.
#   * New src/chaossave.h: the pure parts (tick budget, pass queue, signatures, change test), tested by
#     server/tools/chaossave_test.cpp (CI). Header only: src/CMakeLists.txt is not touched.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0025: patch -p1 < 0026-incremental-save.patch, then rebuild. It touches
# none of the files of 0025, so it also applies without it. The base save.lua is switched to it by
# tools/patch_base_save.py (install_all.py step autosave).
